utils/gpu/with-gpus.py, on a machine of this test's making: its KFD topology,
the GPUs' files in sysfs and one process of another user, under --root. GPU 0
is free; another process has memory on GPU 1; GPU 2 is busy with no process
on it. ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES is unset, as lit passes it on to the tests.

RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/0 %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/1 %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/2 %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/3
RUN: printf 'cpu_cores_count 16\nsimd_count 0\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/0/properties
RUN: printf 'simd_count 416\ngfx_target_version 90010\ndrm_render_minor 128\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/1/properties
RUN: printf '1111\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/1/gpu_id
RUN: printf 'simd_count 416\ngfx_target_version 90010\ndrm_render_minor 129\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/2/properties
RUN: printf '2222\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/2/gpu_id
RUN: printf 'simd_count 1216\ngfx_target_version 90402\ndrm_render_minor 130\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/3/properties
RUN: printf '3333\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/topology/nodes/3/gpu_id
RUN: mkdir -p %t/sys/class/drm/renderD128/device %t/sys/class/drm/renderD129/device %t/sys/class/drm/renderD130/device
RUN: printf '0\n' > %t/sys/class/drm/renderD128/device/gpu_busy_percent
RUN: printf '0\n' > %t/sys/class/drm/renderD129/device/gpu_busy_percent
RUN: printf '90\n' > %t/sys/class/drm/renderD130/device/gpu_busy_percent
RUN: printf '1048576\n' > %t/sys/class/drm/renderD128/device/mem_info_vram_used
RUN: printf '68702699520\n' > %t/sys/class/drm/renderD128/device/mem_info_vram_total
RUN: mkdir -p %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/proc/4242 %t/proc/4242
RUN: printf '0\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/proc/4242/vram_1111
RUN: printf '2147483648\n' > %t/sys/class/kfd/kfd/proc/4242/vram_2222
RUN: printf 'trainer\n' > %t/proc/4242/comm

With no command, it lists the GPUs, numbered as the ROCm runtime numbers
them, which skips the CPU's node.
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LIST --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
LIST:GPU  arch      busy  memory used        other processes
LIST-NEXT:0    gfx90a      0%       1/ 65520 MiB  free
LIST-NEXT:1    gfx90a      0%       0/     0 MiB  busy: {{[^ ]+}} trainer (pid 4242, 2048 MiB)
LIST-NEXT:2    gfx942     90%       0/     0 MiB  busy
LIST-NOT:{{.}}

--count takes free GPUs, and runs the command with ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES set.
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --count 1 -- printenv ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONE --match-full-lines
ONE:with-gpus: ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 (gfx90a)
ONE-NEXT:0
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES not %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --count 2 -- true 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWO
TWO: with-gpus: only 1 of the 2 GPUs asked for are free

--gpus takes the GPUs named, if they are free, or with --force.
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES not %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --gpus 0,1 -- true 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=USED
USED: with-gpus: GPU 1 is in use; --force uses it anyway
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --gpus 0,1 --force --dry-run 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FORCE
FORCE: with-gpus: ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 (gfx90a, gfx90a)
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --max-busy 95 --gpus 2 --dry-run 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MAX
MAX: with-gpus: ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 (gfx942)

A run holds its GPUs until it ends, so another of the user's runs cannot take
them meanwhile.
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --gpus 0 -- env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES not %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --gpus 0 -- true 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HELD
HELD: with-gpus: another of your runs holds GPU 0

Errors.
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES not %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --gpus 5 -- true 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NONE
NONE: with-gpus: there is no GPU 5; the machine has 3
RUN: env ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3 not %with-gpus --root %t --samples 1 --count 1 -- true 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SET
SET: with-gpus: ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES is already set, to 3; unset it, as this script numbers every GPU
RUN: env -u ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES not %with-gpus --root %t/missing --samples 1 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EMPTY
EMPTY: with-gpus: no GPU found in the KFD topology
